4,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/215451132?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fed398472-52a6-4d63-8935-bc77ce98845b_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" title=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-TL7!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fed398472-52a6-4d63-8935-bc77ce98845b_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-TL7!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fed398472-52a6-4d63-8935-bc77ce98845b_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-TL7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fed398472-52a6-4d63-8935-bc77ce98845b_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-TL7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fed398472-52a6-4d63-8935-bc77ce98845b_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>As we closed our Dhammapada-inspired series on Insight Timer last weekend, the final theme of “what truly matters” reminded us of the importance of practice.</p><p>Verses 11 and 12, in Gil Fronsdal’s translation, say that those who mistake the inessential to be essential, and the essential as inessential, never reach the essential. </p><p>Inessential here does not mean bad or wrong. Rather, it points out what is not necessary or not important.</p><p>We are often too close to our own lives to see this. </p><p>So imagine someone else looking at how you spend your time, your energy and your attention. </p><p><em>What would they conclude that you believe matters most?</em></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:205913,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/215451132?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" title=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Tog9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F311330df-9560-423a-9269-50d5c8942338_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>There is usually a gap between what we say matters to us and what our life reveals to matter to us. </p><p>We say family is everything, and then we sit with them without being present. We say we want a simple life, and then we fill every moment with stimulation. We say meditation is a priority, and then we postpone it for everything else.</p><p>So part of the practice is <em>telling the urgent apart from the important</em>. </p><p>Modern life makes everything feel urgent, with the notifications, the updates, and the deadlines. </p><p>What is truly essential tends to come quietly. It is the conversation we keep avoiding, the body that has been struggling in the background. </p><p>It helps to ask: </p><p><em><strong>Does this need my attention because it demands it, or because it truly matters to me?</strong></em></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:345955,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/215451132?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" title=\"Take A Pause - What Truly Matters | Erin Lee Mindful Moments\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rt-W!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc01b5bc3-6c45-4a71-8431-1b69fa51623e_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The final verses turn to reflections on mortality, which is heavy — and meant to be. They are not there to create despair, but drive a <strong>healthy sense of urgency</strong>. </p><p>Time is finite, and a mindful life does not just drop into our lap. We have to cultivate it, and that takes effort and practice.</p><p>This was the closing reflection I left the community with: </p><div class=\"callout-block\" data-callout=\"true\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em><strong>What deserves your limited number of days?</strong></em></p></div><div><hr></div><p>At Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 12-13 September 2026, we reflected on where we would like to expend our time, attention, and energy. We then listened to the poem <a href=\"https://www.awakin.org/v2/read/view.php?tid=477\">When Death Comes</a> by Mary Oliver. </p><h3><strong>Meditation Practice</strong></h3><blockquote><p><em><strong>Tap Play to Practice Together:</strong></em></p></blockquote><div class=\"native-audio-embed\" data-component-name=\"AudioPlaceholder\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;label&quot;:null,&quot;mediaUploadId&quot;:&quot;c2fdac75-f6e9-48c7-9d2b-57138109575e&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1263.7257,&quot;downloadable&quot;:false,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}\"></div><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/what-truly-matters?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">This post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/what-truly-matters?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/what-truly-matters?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><div><hr></div><p></p><p></p>",
  "body_text": "As we closed our Dhammapada-inspired series on Insight Timer last weekend, the final theme of “what truly matters” reminded us of the importance of practice.\n\nVerses 11 and 12, in Gil Fronsdal’s translation, say that those who mistake the inessential to be essential, and the essential as inessential, never reach the essential. \n\nInessential here does not mean bad or wrong. Rather, it points out what is not necessary or not important.\n\nWe are often too close to our own lives to see this. \n\nSo imagine someone else looking at how you spend your time, your energy and your attention. \n\nWhat would they conclude that you believe matters most?\n\nThere is usually a gap between what we say matters to us and what our life reveals to matter to us. \n\nWe say family is everything, and then we sit with them without being present. We say we want a simple life, and then we fill every moment with stimulation. We say meditation is a priority, and then we postpone it for everything else.\n\nSo part of the practice is telling the urgent apart from the important. \n\nModern life makes everything feel urgent, with the notifications, the updates, and the deadlines. \n\nWhat is truly essential tends to come quietly. It is the conversation we keep avoiding, the body that has been struggling in the background. \n\nIt helps to ask: \n\nDoes this need my attention because it demands it, or because it truly matters to me?\n\nThe final verses turn to reflections on mortality, which is heavy — and meant to be. They are not there to create despair, but drive a healthy sense of urgency. \n\nTime is finite, and a mindful life does not just drop into our lap. We have to cultivate it, and that takes effort and practice.\n\nThis was the closing reflection I left the community with: \n\nWhat deserves your limited number of days?\n\n---\n\nAt Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 12-13 September 2026, we reflected on where we would like to expend our time, attention, and energy. We then listened to the poem When Death Comes by Mary Oliver. \n\nMeditation Practice\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---",
